      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1326",
      "html": "<p>Hypostomus hondae (Regan, 1912). Family Loricariidae. Type locality: Honda, Colombia. Maximum size 350 mm SL. IUCN Red List: Not Evaluated.</p><p>Synonyms: Cochliodon hondae, Cochliodon pospisili, Plecostomus hondae.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1326",
      "html": "<p>South America: Magdalena River and Lake Maracaibo basins, and Colombian Caribbean rivers.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1326",
      "html": "<p>Unreported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1326",
      "html": "<p>Previously placed in Cochliodon and now included in the larger genus Hypostomus as a member of the Hypostomus Cochliodon group. All these species have higher backs than other related species and spoon-shaped teeth (like Panaque).</p><p>Etymology: Greek hypo = under + Greek stoma = mouth. Named after the river Honda where the type specimen was captured.</p>"
    },
    {
